# This file is COMMIT #1, deliberately, before any generated file exists.
#
# Why it is load-bearing: on Windows `core.autocrlf=true` is a common default. Without
# these rules, git checks out CRLF while every generator (buf, protoc-gen-go, gofmt)
# writes LF. That silently breaks:
#   - tools/codegen_uptodate_test.go  (regenerates to a temp dir and byte-compares)
#   - every golden-file test
#   - gofmt -l / golangci-lint in CI
# The failure is red on a fresh clone for a reason the cloner cannot diagnose.
#
# test/repohygiene_test.go asserts no tracked text file contains CRLF, so this file
# cannot silently stop working.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.go        text eol=lf
*.mod       text eol=lf
*.sum       text eol=lf
*.proto     text eol=lf
*.sql       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.json      text eol=lf
*.md        text eol=lf
*.txt       text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf

# Generated code: collapse in PR diffs and exclude from language statistics.
gen/** linguist-generated=true

# Golden files are byte-exact contracts. Never let git touch their bytes.
*.golden           -text
testdata/golden/** -text

*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.ico   binary
*.binpb binary
